  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "SCR-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-cusp-mobius-reduction",
      "title": "Möbius action on the Hilbert upper half-plane, norm-square product, and balanced height lower bound",
      "statement": "For any totally real number field F with real embeddings ρ_w and any point τ in the product upper half-plane ℍ^[F:ℚ], the componentwise fractional-linear action of SL₂(F) has nowhere-vanishing denominators, preserves positive imaginary parts with Im((γ · τ)_w) = Im(τ_w) / |ρ_w(c) τ_w + ρ_w(d)|², defines a left group action of SL₂(F), and acts by translation τ_w + ρ_w(b), quadratic scaling ρ_w(a)² τ_w, and inversion −τ_w⁻¹ on the unipotent, diagonal, and Weyl generators. Moreover, ∏_w ρ_w(x)² = N_(F/ℚ)(x)² for every x ∈ F, and any balanced family of positive heights z_w > 0 with κ z_w ≤ z_v and ∏_v z_v ≥ P satisfies z_w ≥ κ min(1, P) at every real place w.",
      "hypotheses": "Number field F (totally real for the embedding norm-square identity and Siegel-domain reduction), real embeddings ρ_w : F → ℝ compatible with the archimedean places of F, and τ_w ∈ ℂ with Im τ_w > 0 for every infinite place w. For the balanced lower bound, any finite nonempty index set of places, positive heights z_w > 0, balance constant κ > 0, and product floor P ∈ ℝ.",
      "correspondence": "The fractional-linear identities hold coordinatewise from determinant one and give the exact generator formulas used for cusp reduction and modular automorphy. Together with the norm-square product over real embeddings and the elementary contradiction deducing uniform height floors from unit balance and product bounds, these lemmas supply the algebraic and real-analytic base of Siegel-domain reduction.",
      "dependencies": [],
