    {
      "id": "SCR-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-adelic-weil-orbit",
      "title": "Adelic Weil datum, finite-adelic Iwasawa factorization, theta and Eisenstein automorphy, and inverse-denominator decay",
      "statement": "For a totally real number field F, a standard finite-adelic additive character ψ, and a symmetric invertible quadratic matrix B of size 2M over F with positive-definite majorants P_w satisfying P_w B_w⁻¹ P_w = B_w, the rescaled product Haar measure μ_f = |disc F|^(−M) |N_(F/ℚ)(det B)|^(−1/2) λ_f^(⊗2M) satisfies self-duality on every compact open subgroup and yields a complete non-archimedean Weil representation datum. Every rational element b ∈ F admits a constructive finite-adelic Iwasawa factorization w n(b) = n(y) m(a) k with k ∈ SL₂(Ô_F) and a Ô_F = {x ∈ Ô_F : b x ∈ Ô_F} of normalized Haar measure den(b)⁻¹. Combining the principal congruence neighborhood basis N Ô_F^(2M), the finite-orbit uniform bound under SL₂(Ô_F), and Haar scaling yields |f*(φ, b)| ≤ C · den(b)^(−M) for every Schwartz–Bruhat test φ and every b ∈ F. Furthermore, the quadratic theta series θ(φ; τ) is absolutely summable (and nonvanishing for a suitable congruence indicator), transforms covariantly under rational translations, rational dilations, and Weyl inversion with the archimedean factor c_G(τ), and for M ≥ 3 the adelic Eisenstein series obeys the exact same SL₂(F) automorphy laws.",
      "hypotheses": "Totally real number field F, normalized additive Haar measure λ_f on the finite adeles 𝔸_(F,f) with λ_f(Ô_F) = 1, continuous standard additive character ψ on 𝔸_(F,f) agreeing with exp(−2πi Tr_(F/ℚ)(b)) on F, symmetric nonsingular matrix B of size 2M over F, positive-definite real majorants P_w satisfying P_w B_w⁻¹ P_w = B_w, orthogonal pair (g_f, g_∞) preserving B, locally constant compactly supported test φ on 𝔸_(F,f)^(2M), and τ ∈ ℍ^[F:ℚ]; M ≥ 3 for the Eisenstein series automorphy.",
      "correspondence": "Open subgroups of Ô_F have Haar measure inverse to their ideal index in 𝒪_F, which evaluates both denominator lattices and global linear Jacobians by diagonal-transvection induction. The idempotent-and-scale matrix factorization w n(b) = n(y) m(a) k puts m(a⁻¹) n(−y) w n(b) inside SL₂(Ô_F) and extracts the sharp den(b)^(−M) decay directly from the finite-orbit uniform bound. For theta functions, denominator clearing gives Gaussian summability, the global product formula gives parabolic invariance, and Poisson summation on shifted level lattices gives Weyl inversion.",
      "dependencies": [
        "SCR-01"
      ],
