    {
      "id": "SCR-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-parabolic-quotient-volumes",
      "title": "Split-extension parabolic Haar measure, triviality of the conjugation modular character, and finite-covolume quotient unfolding",
      "statement": "Let 1 → N → P ⇄ G₁ → 1 be a continuously split exact sequence of locally compact second-countable Hausdorff topological groups with section ι : G₁ → P and projection π : P → G₁, and let Γ ⊂ P be a discrete countable subgroup projecting into a countable lattice Γ₁ ⊂ G₁ with ι(Γ₁) ⊂ Γ. Suppose G₁ has a finite-covolume fundamental domain 𝓕₁ for Γ₁ with respect to a left Haar measure μ₁, and Γ ∩ N is cocompact in N = ker π. Then N carries a left Haar measure ν and a measurable strict fundamental domain D for Γ ∩ N with 0 < ν(D) < ∞, conjugation by ι(G₁) preserves ν identically because the induced measurable modular character δ : G₁ → ℝ≥0 is trivial on the finite-covolume lattice Γ₁ and is therefore identically 1, the pushforward μ_P = Φ_*(ν ⊗ μ₁) under Φ(m, u) = m · ι(u) is a left Haar measure on P, and 𝓕_P = Φ(D × 𝓕₁) is a fundamental domain for Γ in P of finite covolume μ_P(𝓕_P) = ν(D) μ₁(𝓕₁) < ∞ satisfying ∫_(𝓕_P) f dμ_P = ∫_(𝓕₁) ∫_D f(m · ι(u)) dν(m) dμ₁(u) for every measurable f : P → [0, ∞].",
      "hypotheses": "Locally compact second-countable Hausdorff topological groups P and G₁ equipped with Borel sigma-algebras, continuous homomorphisms ι : G₁ → P and π : P → G₁ with π(ι(u)) = u, countable subgroups Γ ⊂ P and Γ₁ ⊂ G₁ such that Γ is discrete in P, ι(Γ₁) ⊂ Γ, π(Γ) ⊂ Γ₁, μ₁ is a left Haar measure on G₁ with fundamental domain 𝓕₁ of finite measure, and a compact set K ⊂ P meets every (Γ ∩ N)-coset in N = ker π.",
      "correspondence": "The split homeomorphism Φ : N × G₁ ≃ₜ P converts left multiplication in P into semidirect conjugation on N times left translation on G₁. Cocompactness of Γ ∩ N yields a measurable strict section D of finite positive measure, whose stability under conjugation by ι(Γ₁) forces the conjugation Haar character δ to equal 1 on Γ₁. Partitioning G₁ into logarithmic shells t^n ≤ δ(u) < t^(n+1) shows any measurable homomorphism trivial on a finite-covolume lattice is identically 1, making μ_P = Φ_*(ν ⊗ μ₁) left-invariant and enabling Tonelli unfolding on 𝓕_P = Φ(D × 𝓕₁).",
      "dependencies": [
        "SCR-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-parabolic-split-unfold-eq"
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "declaration": "GlobalTheory.CompanionTheory.SplitExtLat.splitHomeo",
          "declaration_lines": {
